resources.string:
On the Configs tab tap a card to make that config active — the VPN connects with it.

The ⋮ menu of a config:
• Edit — change the TOML by hand;
• Show QR code — move it to another device (the code contains the password, show it only to people you trust);
• Update from dashboard — for configs from a link;
• Delete.

Configs from the dashboard cannot be edited or shown as a QR code: the server issues and updates them.

Rules → Apps (or the card on the main screen). Modes:
• All apps through VPN — the default;
• Selected apps bypass VPN — checked apps go directly, e.g. a bank or games;
• Only selected apps through VPN — only checked apps use the VPN.

The list has search and filters. System apps (Google services, WebView and others) are hidden — turn on the System filter. Only apps that can use the internet are listed.

Changes apply on the next connection. FireTunnel itself always bypasses the VPN.

Rules → Sites and addresses. Modes:
• Don\'t use the list — routing as set in the config;
• Bypass the VPN — everything through the VPN except the list;
• Only through the VPN — only the list goes through the VPN.

Add domains (example.com, *.example.com), IP addresses and subnets (10.0.0.0/8): one per line or by importing a text list from a link. Invalid lines are skipped. Each entry can be switched off temporarily.

The list is added to the config\'s settings when connecting.

Settings → Appearance:
• theme — as in the system, light or dark;
• Wallpaper colours (Android 12+) — colours follow the wallpaper;
• Colour scheme — Fire, Ocean, Forest or Amethyst; available when wallpaper colours are off.

Changes apply at once.

Won\'t connect:
• check the internet without the VPN;
• look at the server ping — “no response” means the server is unreachable from this network;
• if the config uses HTTP/3, try HTTP/2: some networks block QUIC;
• turn on Anti-DPI in the constructor\'s advanced settings.

Sites don\'t open although the VPN is connected: check the mode on the Rules tab and the DNS in the config.

A dashboard config disappeared: the device was removed or access was revoked — get a new link in the dashboard.

An app is missing from the list: turn on the System filter — services and apps without a launcher icon are there.
